  "id": "DrugBank_DB03904 - MONDO_4980",
  "verbalization": "Urea appears to be a potential candidate for repurposing in the treatment of atopic eczema, as it is linked through a series of indications to dermatitis, which in turn is associated with atopic eczema. The evidence suggests that Urea may exert a therapeutic effect through a pathway involving dermatitis, with Crisaborole and Pimecrolimus acting as intermediaries in this relationship. These agents are commonly used in the management of atopic eczema, and their association with the condition implies a possible mechanism of action that could be shared by Urea. The overlapping indications and the presence of multiple pathways linking Urea to atopic eczema highlight a potential for Urea to be repurposed in this context, though further studies are needed to confirm the direct therapeutic effect of Urea on atopic eczema.",
